# Line endings are part of what ships: the skill and plugin files are
# embedded into the binary byte for byte, and a CRLF checkout would embed
# different bytes than the ones that were reviewed and ship an installation
# whose rendered files differ from the goldens the tests hold them to.
# Everything text stays LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# CRLF bytes are this fixture's subject, and its checksum and test depend on
# them; text=auto would normalize them to LF on the next `git add`.
testdata/fixtures/sse/crlf_endings.sse -text
# The same for a Codex config golden whose subject is a participant's CRLF
# lines surviving an install and an uninstall byte for byte.
cmd/jevlin/testdata/codex/states/default-permissions-workspace-crlf.after.toml -text
*.png binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
